11 Brown Adipocyte Respiration Protocol: Prepare cells as described in the first two steps of the intact brown adipocyte respiration protocol. On the day of the experiment, thaw 1x MAS and pre-made substrate solutions. Prepare 10x solutions of inhibitors in 1x MAS. If using fatty acid substrates, prepare them freshly as described. Soak the cartridge for at least 3 hours before loading. Load specified volumes into ports A-D and calibrate the cartridge. Prepare $7.5\mathrm{mM}$ PMP in 1x MAS, gently wash cells with 1x MAS once, completely evacuate the wash, and add $450~\mu 1$ 1x MAS with $7.5\mathrm{nM}$ PMP. Perform the Seahorse assay with 2-3 measurements per condition, ensuring not to exceed 1 hour before injecting Antimycin A to maintain mitochondrial integrity.   
